# T53 twisted Bloch sectors (note 35 §5). Script: t27_minimizer_regularity.py,
# modes "twist L n0 theta_spec ndir rows=..." and "twistcheck". Each row line gives the
# exact-flux row norm s as a bracket [lo, hi] (lo: polygon LP with ndir directions;
# hi: complex l1 norm of the LP residual). theta=diag:t is (t,t,t,t); x:t is (t,0,0,0).
# At theta = 0 with ndir = 4 the value is exact. rows=orbits: one row per orbit of the axis
# permutations (S_4 for diag/0, S_3 on axes 1-3 for x), so "max over" = s_L on that torus.
# Row index u = ((u0 L + u1) L + u2) L + u3; a indexes (01, 02, 03, 12, 13, 23). t = elapsed s.

## twistcheck
theta=0 row equals T27 reindexed row: max diff 7.9e-17
theta=2pi row equals theta=0 row: max diff 8.6e-17
D at 2pi equals D at 0: 2.4e-16
twisted row reproduces the multiplier on twisted plane waves: max diff 8.7e-16
D_theta annihilates twisted curls: 2.7e-15
dim ker D_theta = 768, dim exact = 3 n0^4 = 768

